        "original_id": "35759072-a0d2-5800-8023-a2c4dad1589a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Cleek-McCabe Site, Walton, Boone County, Kentucky, Bluegrass region\n- Concepts: Middle Fort Ancient culture, archaeology, geographic regions\n\nFacts:\n- The Cleek-McCabe Site is an archaeological site near Walton in Boone County, Kentucky.\n- The Cleek-McCabe Site is associated with the Middle Fort Ancient culture from 1200 to 1400 CE.\n- The Bluegrass region, called Eskippakithiki in Shawnee, is a geographic region in Kentucky.\n- The Bluegrass region forms the northern part of Kentucky.\n- A majority of Kentucky's population has lived in the Bluegrass region, and the state's largest cities developed there.\n- The Cleek-McCabe Site is located in Kentucky's northern Bluegrass region.",
